Undockerize + Multi-CA Plan (Part 2)

Goals
- [ ] Support multiple independent CAs on a single host without Docker volumes.
- [ ] Use XDG data dir for CA state and XDG config dir for a registry of CAs and defaults.
- [ ] Make `init` accept an identifier and optional .env to initialize a named CA.
- [ ] Add `list`, `export`, `import`, and `use` commands; deprecate `eject`/`re-init` with aliases.
- [ ] Require an explicit CA selection for operations that depend on a CA (`issue`, `cert-manager`, `validate`) unless a default is set.
- [ ] Ensure OpenSSL configs point to the per-CA directories (no hard-coded /opt paths).

Design
- [ ] XDG locations
  - [ ] Data: base data dir default `DATA_HOME=${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}`; `CA_DATA_ROOT=${DATA_HOME}/simple-ca`.
  - [ ] Config: `CONF_HOME=${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}`; `CA_CONFIG_DIR=${CONF_HOME}/simple_ca`; registry file `config.json`.
  - [ ] Export root: keep `exportDir` defaulting to `${CA_DATA_ROOT}/export`, but write per-CA into `${exportDir}/${CA_ID}/` to avoid collisions.
- [ ] Per-CA layout (under `${CA_DATA_ROOT}/cas/${CA_ID}`):
  - [ ] `root/{private,certs,crl,newcerts}` + db files in `root/` (`index.txt`, `serial`, `crlnumber`)
  - [ ] `intermediate/{private,certs,crl,newcerts,csr}` + db files in `intermediate/`
  - [ ] `output/<CN>/...` for issued artifacts (as today)
  - [ ] `config/.env` snapshot of inputs used for this CA (optional); `config/meta.json` (derived)
  - [ ] `openssl-root.cnf` and `openssl-intermediate.cnf` generated with correct `dir =` pointing to the per-CA dirs (these are working copies, not templates)
- [ ] Registry file `${CA_CONFIG_DIR}/config.json` structure (authoritative CA inventory):
  - [ ] JSON object with keys:
    - [ ] `defaultCa` (string | null)
    - [ ] `cas` (object map of `${CA_ID}` → { id, name?, org?, createdAt, dataPath, exportPath })
  - [ ] Avoid runtime JSON mutation complexity: if `jq` is available, use it to mutate; otherwise fall back to read-only operations and derive list by directory scan.
- [ ] CA identifier rules
  - [ ] Allowed: `[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{1,62}` (lowercase, digits, `-`, `_`); reject others.
  - [ ] `--ca` selects CA; `--ca-id` used only at `init`/`import` time to create/register a new one.

CLI changes
- [ ] Global flags (in `src/main.sh`):
  - [ ] `--ca <id>`: select CA for the subcommand; if omitted, use `defaultCa` from registry; if still none, error for CA-dependent commands.
  - [ ] `--config <path>`: optional path to alternate registry file; default `${CA_CONFIG_DIR}/config.json`.
  - [ ] Keep `--base-path` and `--export-dir` as overrides; when a CA is selected, resolve them as roots and then scope to CA (`${basePath}/cas/${CA_ID}`, `${exportDir}/${CA_ID}`).
- [ ] New commands:
  - [ ] `list`: enumerate registered CAs with id, dataPath, default marker; if registry missing and no jq, scan `${CA_DATA_ROOT}/cas/*`.
  - [ ] `use --ca <id>`: set default CA in registry.
  - [ ] `export --ca <id> [-o file.tar.gz]`: archive the CA data dir + per-CA config; default output under `${exportDir}/${CA_ID}/<caId>-YYYYmmddHHMMSS.tar.gz`.
  - [ ] `import --ca-id <id> -i file.tar.gz [--force]`: create CA dir, extract archive, register in registry; fail if exists unless `--force`.
- [ ] Updated commands:
  - [ ] `init`: require `--ca-id <id>`; accept `--env-file <path>` to source inputs; snapshot to `${caDir}/config/.env` and register in registry.
  - [ ] `issue`, `validate`, `cert-manager`: require CA selection via `--ca` or default; write exports to `${exportDir}/${CA_ID}/`.
  - [ ] `eject` → alias of `export`; `re-init` → alias of `import` (keep for backward-compat, warn).

OpenSSL config handling
- [ ] Keep `src/openssl-*.cnf` as templates.
- [ ] On `init` (and if missing on first use), write per-CA working copies:
  - [ ] `${caDir}/root/openssl-root.cnf` with `dir = ${caDir}/root`.
  - [ ] `${caDir}/intermediate/openssl-intermediate.cnf` with `dir = ${caDir}/intermediate`.
- [ ] Commands use the per-CA working copies if present; otherwise generate them on-the-fly from templates (idempotent).

Implementation tasks
- [ ] New file: `src/config.sh`
  - [ ] Functions: `config_path`, `ensure_config_dir`, `load_registry`, `save_registry`, `registry_list`, `registry_get_default`, `registry_set_default`, `registry_register_ca`, `registry_remove_ca`.
  - [ ] If `jq` present, implement JSON read/write; else, minimal read-only: detect CAs by scanning `${CA_DATA_ROOT}/cas/*` and treat default as unset.
- [ ] Update `src/common.sh`
  - [ ] Compute `default_xdg_data_dir` and `CA_DATA_ROOT` as above.
  - [ ] If `--ca` selected or default present, set `CA_ID` and compute:
    - [ ] `caDir=${basePath}/cas/${CA_ID}`
    - [ ] `rootCAPath=${caDir}/root`
    - [ ] `intermediatePath=${caDir}/intermediate`
    - [ ] `exportDir=${exportDir}/${CA_ID}` (scoped)
  - [ ] Provide `require_ca_selected` helper to error if `CA_ID` is not set for CA-dependent commands.
  - [ ] Provide `ensure_per_ca_openssl_configs` helper that writes missing working copies from templates.
- [ ] Update `src/main.sh`
  - [ ] Parse `--ca`, `--config` as global flags; export `CA_ID` and `REGISTRY_PATH`.
  - [ ] Add subcommands `list`, `use`, `export`, `import` and wire to new/renamed scripts.
  - [ ] Update help text to document multi-CA, defaults, XDG paths.
- [ ] Update `src/init.sh`
  - [ ] Options: `--ca-id <id>` (required), `--env-file <path>`, plus existing key options.
  - [ ] Load `--env-file` before computing subjects; validate id; fail if CA exists unless `--force`.
  - [ ] Create `${caDir}` structure; generate per-CA openssl configs; write keys/certs into those dirs.
  - [ ] Snapshot `.env` to `${caDir}/config/.env`; create `meta.json` with minimal fields (id, createdAt, org, subject DN); register in registry file.
- [ ] Update `src/request-server-cert.sh`
  - [ ] Call `require_ca_selected` early.
  - [ ] Use per-CA working `openssl-intermediate.cnf` (generate if missing).
  - [ ] Write exports to `${exportDir}/${CA_ID}/`; ensure dirs exist; prefer `0644` for public artifacts, `0600` for private.
- [ ] Update `src/validate.sh`, `src/cert-manager.sh`
  - [ ] Accept/use `--ca`; scope outputs to `${exportDir}/${CA_ID}/`.
- [ ] Replace/alias scripts
  - [ ] New `src/list.sh`: prints table/json with `id`, `dataPath`, `default` marker.
  - [ ] New `src/use.sh`: sets default in registry.
  - [ ] New `src/export.sh`: archives selected CA dir.
  - [ ] New `src/import.sh`: imports archive into new/existing id.
  - [ ] Keep `eject-ca.sh` and `re-init.sh` as thin shims printing deprecation notice and exec into `export.sh`/`import.sh`.

Migration & compatibility
- [ ] On first run, if `${basePath}/root` and `${basePath}/intermediate` exist and `${basePath}/cas` is empty:
  - [ ] Offer to register a legacy CA as `default` (or `legacy`); do not move files automatically; create a registry entry pointing `dataPath` at `${basePath}`.
  - [ ] Subsequent operations with `--ca default` continue to work against legacy layout; `list` shows it with a `(legacy)` tag.
  - [ ] Provide `simpleca migrate --ca-id <id>` later to move into `${basePath}/cas/<id>` (tracked separately).
- [ ] Docker: keep current ENV defaults; no behavior change required; commands gain `--ca`.

Tests (bats)
- [ ] Unit
  - [ ] `main` global flags: `--ca`, `--config` parsing.
  - [ ] `list` enumerates registered and/or scanned CAs.
  - [ ] `use` sets default; `issue`/`validate` use default when `--ca` omitted.
  - [ ] `init --ca-id` creates correct layout and registers CA.
  - [ ] `issue --ca <id>` writes artifacts under the scoped export dir.
  - [ ] Back-compat: `eject` and `re-init` route to new commands.
- [ ] Integration
  - [ ] Create two CAs (`acme`, `beta`) with different `.env`; issue certs for both; verify chains.
  - [ ] `export` one CA, delete it, `import` back; `list` reflects changes.
  - [ ] Legacy detection path: simulate old layout; `list` shows legacy; `issue --ca default` still works.

Acceptance criteria
- [ ] Multiple CAs can be initialized and used concurrently under `${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/simple-ca/cas/<id>`.
- [ ] `simpleca list` shows all CAs; `simpleca use --ca <id>` sets default; `issue`/`cert-manager` require `--ca` or use default.
- [ ] `simpleca export --ca <id>` creates a tarball containing the CA dir and per-CA configs under `${exportDir}/${id}/`.
- [ ] `simpleca import --ca-id <id> -i <archive>` registers and restores a CA; refuses overwrite unless `--force`.
- [ ] OpenSSL operations use per-CA config files pointing at the correct directories; no references to `/opt/` remain in logic paths (OK in templates).
- [ ] All new/updated scripts pass `shellcheck`; new unit/integration tests pass via `make test`.
